      "writtenOn": "2026-07-16T15:56:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`af_xdp_remove_program()` only returns an error code, so this path leaves `args-\u003erv` and `args-\u003eerror` unchanged. Since multi-buffer creation always selects a default program, a detach failure can make the CLI/API report success even though creation aborted. Also, if the rollback at `err2` fails, the unregistered device is retained with no way to retry deletion. Could we propagate the detach error and handle the rollback result here?",
      "revId": "9b462ba935bb6505004a6c5c489042f4cbbb4376",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
